---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import ReleaseModel from "../../components/exhibits/ReleaseModel.astro";
---
<Docs title="Changelog" lede="Every release, newest first, on the history wall.">
  <ReleaseModel slot="exhibit" />
  <section class="ply-wall ply-wide" aria-label="Releases">
    <div class="ply-wall__year">
      <p class="ply-wall__label">0.2</p>
      <ul class="ply-wall__entries">
        <li class="ply-pub">
          <p class="ply-pub__title">0.2.0, fixes from an accessibility audit</p>
          <p class="ply-pub__venue">11 October 2026</p>
          <div class="ply-prose ply-small" style="margin-top: var(--ply-space-2)">
            <ul>
              <li>The Astro components load their scripts from <code>dist/js</code>. In 0.1.4, six of them (ThemeToggle, Machine, Complex, Code, Slider, Toc) imported files the npm package leaves out, so a site that installed from npm failed to build. <code>npm run check:package</code> now fails CI when a packaged file points at something the package does not ship.</li>
              <li>A hovered button fills with <code>--ply-color-accent-text</code> and labels with the new <code>--ply-color-on-accent</code>, which keeps 4.5:1 in both themes.</li>
              <li>Inside panels and code blocks, muted text and the focus ring take their panel values. On mustard notes the ring is black. Mark other surfaces with <code>data-surface="panel"</code> or <code>data-surface="note"</code>.</li>
              <li>Windows contrast themes keep checks, radio balls, switches, the current tab, and status marks visible. Pages print in the light theme with ink-on-white panels.</li>
              <li>On touch screens, small controls grow to 44px. The top bar and the pager fit at 320px.</li>
              <li>Citation cards no longer widen the page on phones, stay open under the pointer, and close with Escape (<code>js/cite.js</code>).</li>
              <li>A machine that starts by itself finishes within five seconds. Changing its attributes no longer fires <code>ply-machine-done</code>, and its label reads out the counts.</li>
              <li>Sliders set <code>aria-valuetext</code>, the loading indicator announces its text, and the theme toggle is a "Dark theme" toggle button.</li>
              <li><code>PaperHeader</code> and <code>AppShell</code> take a <code>level</code> prop for their heading. Sidenotes stay inline when the main column has no room for the margin.</li>
              <li>New token <code>--ply-size-ui</code> (15px) for tabs, tables, notes, and sidebar links. Chart text uses <code>--ply-size-xs</code>.</li>
              <li>Titles no longer jump when Ultra arrives. A new <code>Ultra Fallback</code> face scales Georgia Bold to Ultra's metrics, and the display stack lists it right after Ultra.</li>
              <li>To update: <code>Status</code> is a live region only with <code>live</code>, so add it where a script changes a status outside an app shell. The <code>kbd</code> and <code>blockquote</code> element defaults moved to the base layer, and any class now wins over them.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="ply-wall__year">
      <p class="ply-wall__label">0.1</p>
      <ul class="ply-wall__entries">
        <li class="ply-pub">
          <p class="ply-pub__title">0.1.4, on npm and PyPI</p>
          <p class="ply-pub__venue">11 October 2026</p>
          <div class="ply-prose ply-small" style="margin-top: var(--ply-space-2)">
            <ul>
              <li>Polytope is published as <code>@dario-loi/polytope</code> on npm and <code>polytope-theme</code> on PyPI. Installs need no <code>.npmrc</code> line, and upgrades work with <code>npm update</code>.</li>
              <li>The design command runs as <code>npx @dario-loi/polytope</code>, which can only ever fetch this package.</li>
              <li>A release workflow publishes both packages from GitHub releases through trusted publishing, with npm provenance.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ply-pub">
          <p class="ply-pub__title">0.1.3, no install scripts</p>
          <p class="ply-pub__venue">11 October 2026</p>
          <div class="ply-prose ply-small" style="margin-top: var(--ply-space-2)">
            <ul>
              <li>The built <code>dist/</code> is now committed and the <code>prepare</code> script is gone, so installing from GitHub runs no install scripts. npm 12 no longer prints the "install scripts blocked" warning, and nothing needs approving.</li>
              <li>CI rebuilds and fails if the committed <code>dist/</code> differs from a fresh build.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ply-pub">
          <p class="ply-pub__title">0.1.2, safer install commands</p>
          <p class="ply-pub__venue">11 October 2026</p>
          <div class="ply-prose ply-small" style="margin-top: var(--ply-space-2)">
            <ul>
              <li>Install commands quote the git address, since zsh reads an unquoted <code>#</code> as a glob pattern.</li>
              <li>The docs and the command's own messages no longer suggest <code>npx polytope-design</code>, which falls back to the public npm registry when the package is missing. Use <code>./node_modules/.bin/polytope-design</code> or an <code>npm run</code> script.</li>
              <li>A no-npm path for static sites: fetch <code>DESIGN.md</code> and <code>design.json</code> pinned to a release tag.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ply-pub">
          <p class="ply-pub__title">0.1.1, the design record ships</p>
          <p class="ply-pub__venue">11 October 2026</p>
          <div class="ply-prose ply-small" style="margin-top: var(--ply-space-2)">
            <ul>
              <li>The package now includes <code>DESIGN.md</code> and <code>design.json</code>, the files Impeccable reads to know a project's visual system.</li>
              <li>New command <code>polytope-design</code> copies them into a site; <code>--check</code> reports a stale copy.</li>
              <li>CI runs on Node 24 and the current GitHub action versions.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="ply-pub">
          <p class="ply-pub__title">0.1.0, first release</p>
          <p class="ply-pub__venue">11 October 2026</p>
          <div class="ply-prose ply-small" style="margin-top: var(--ply-space-2)">
            <ul>
              <li>Tokens in the W3C format, compiled to CSS, JavaScript and TypeScript, JSON, Sass, Tailwind v4, LaTeX, a code theme, and Python.</li>
              <li>CSS core in cascade layers, with light and dark themes and self-hosted fonts.</li>
              <li>Components for buttons, navigation, notes, forms, tables, code, research pages, long-form writing, demos, and charts.</li>
              <li>Two working models: the probability machine and the complex.</li>
              <li>32 Astro components.</li>
              <li>Python theme for matplotlib, plotly, Gradio, and Streamlit.</li>
              <li>This site, with three pattern pages.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Docs>
